--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Media Engine audio offload
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
PSPATTERN runs its send-effects bank (a feedback delay and an FDN reverb)
on the PSP's second Allegrex core, the Media Engine. To our knowledge this
is the first live audio-effects bank to run on the Media Engine inside a
music application. The offload design and DSP are original work by
HobbyChop: the cross-core hand-off and wet ring, the FPU
flush-to-zero for the Media Engine's missing denormal hardware, and the
uncached line handling.

It builds on the Media Engine access library by mcidclan (m-c/d),
psp-media-engine-custom-core, which handles Media Engine boot, kernel
access, and standby. That library is MIT licensed and vendored under
third_party/me-core/ with its original LICENSE.md preserved:

